WEBVTT

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.690
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.980
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.540
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.790
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.390
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:40.700
aoku hatenai sora no katasumi de
Newborn in a corner of the endless blue sky...

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:43.980
umareta yume ga
The dream is there,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:47.110
ima chiisakutemo
and even though it may now be small...

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.980
koori tsuku you na
No matter how strong they may blow...

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.960
tsuyoi kaze de sae
...or how icy they may be...

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.730
sono mune ni kagayaku
...those winds can never erase...

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:04.160
yume o keshitari, sou yo
...the dream that shines. Oh, no!

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.670
keshitari nante dekinai
The dream that shines inside your heart!

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.900
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:15.100
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.700
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.940
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.320
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.600
<i>04th Team!</i>
<i>You ready to move out yet?!</i>

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.740
<i>You guys are way</i>
<i>behind schedule!</i>

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.910
Okay, stop it there!
Lock it down!

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:20.800
Move it! Move it!

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.910
You want those fags in the
07th team to beat us?!

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.310
Hey, Pietro! Make sure you
come back in one piece!

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.530
I will if you have the
money I won last night!

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.680
I hope you get
eaten by dogs!

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.120
Clear the path, you idiots!

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.840
- Unit two, cut the chatter!
- Right, right.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.540
And away they go.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.320
You drinking on
the job again, Gramps?

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:50.250
Karen, your new commander
still hasn't shown up?

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:53.880
No. Probably
playing big shot...

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.740
What happened to that
straight-arrow you had?

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.020
In a hospital
on the rear line.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.150
They say he had
a nervous breakdown.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.130
- Which you caused.
- What was that?!

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.200
Oh, nothin'! Nothin'!

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.000
Eledore!

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.540
You gonna answer me or not?!

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.420
Is she nuts?

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.780
Oh, yeah!
Struck it rich again!

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.920
Again?! Christ,
what's with you today?

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.430
Yeah. You better watch your
back once we're Earthside!

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:44.330
C'mon, lay off.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.520
It's so big!

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:56.190
Doesn't look anything
like it does from Side 2.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.150
Hey, take a look at this, too.
It's the Earth! The Earth!

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.490
All right...

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.320
It's incredible!
Huge! Beautiful!

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.420
Just seeing it makes
you excited! Right?

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.930
Because you're going
there to fight?

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.520
Of course!

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.990
I'm going to drive
the Zeon off of Earth.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.950
Drive them off?

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:26.230
I'll do it, too. I'll take out as
many Zeon soldiers as I can!

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:29.770
Hey, is this your first
time Earthside, too?

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.140
You, too, Ensign?

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.650
Well, yeah.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:39.290
<i>B.B., I'm on my way to Earth now with</i>
<i>some other Federal Forces soldiers.</i>

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.200
What? You mean none of you
have rehearsed for this?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:49.590
Come on! We don't need to
for fighting the Zeeks!

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.960
<i>It's disgraceful!</i>

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:56.000
<i>This Ensign Shiro Amada</i>
<i>I'm traveling with...</i>

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:58.600
<i>He seems to have</i>
<i>some combat experience...</i>

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:02.080
<i>...but he doesn't take the</i>
<i>coming battle seriously at all.</i>

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.410
<i>He acts like he's</i>
<i>going on a picnic!</i>

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:09.680
<i>But don't worry, B.B. I'll be</i>
<i>coming back from this alive!</i>

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:14.830
What's that?

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.430
It's a signal flare!

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:17.720
A signal flare?

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.460
It can't be!

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:26.360
Those are explosions!
It's a battle!

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:30.440
What is this shit? I thought
this area was under Fed control!

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:31.970
It can't be a battle!

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.690
But, just now...
There they are!

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.240
Outta the way!

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.450
That GM's been hit!

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:02.740
Goddamn Zeeks!

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:04.340
That's an improved Zaku!

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.050
I hope they don't
come this way.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.970
The last thing we need is
to get caught up in that!

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.710
Caught up in it?

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:14.280
He <i>is</i> sending
out a mayday, but...

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.910
Let's go and help him!

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:19.150
Ensign, this ship wouldn't
be any good in a battle.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:24.820
There must be <i>something</i>
we can do. Something...

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.390
It's no use.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:29.160
If we had a mobile suit,
it'd be different, but...

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.900
The Ball! I saw one
when I came aboard!

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.260
The Ball?

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:36.260
It has a 15 caliber
gun on it, but...

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:39.180
That'll do just fine!
Please, let me use it!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.140
What can you hope to
do with that thing?

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:45.710
What if you mess up and
put my ship in danger?

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:48.250
Besides, we can't
change course.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:50.010
Despite that, you still
want to go out?

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.350
Yes, sir!
Please let me do it!

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.220
- H- Hey, wait!
- What?

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.360
Where do you think you're going?

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:01.530
To help that pilot!
Now watch me!

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:04.730
- Help him?
- He's taking the BALL out?!

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.450
We don't want to get involved!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.740
<i>I can't just stand by and</i>
<i>let one of our guys get killed!</i>

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.780
<i>We're sending you out.</i>
<i>Ready to go?</i>

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:16.510
Aye, sir!

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:17.800
<i>Opening hatch!</i>

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.440
Ready when you are.

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:21.510
<i>I don't want any</i>
<i>more repeats of Side 2!</i>

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:29.950
<i>Disengage locks, please.</i>

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:30.970
<i>Disengaging.</i>

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.550
<i>Unlocking, confirmed!</i>
<i>Exiting bay!</i>

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:43.110
I've cleared the bay!

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.220
Where are they?
Where did they go?!

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:14.960
There!

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.710
G- God dammit!
If I just had some ammo!

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:27.350
Has my dumb luck
finally run out?

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.060
<i>Don't move...</i>

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.000
A Ball?!

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.680
<i>If you can move,</i>
<i>then get out of here!</i>

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:12.990
<i>There's a transport holding</i>
<i>at 8 o'clock, moonward!</i>

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:18.700
You can't take that
thing in a Ball! Leave me!

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:21.450
<i>Quit talking tough!</i>
<i>Now get going!!!</i>

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:24.640
There! Now you can't move!

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.050
Will it hold?!

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:03.220
Dammit!

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:12.850
A woman?

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.450
I'm sure that was a woman!

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.250
<i>Can't believe you made</i>
<i>it back in this thing!</i>

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:54.700
<i>Hey, move it!</i>
<i>And watch those flashes!</i>

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:56.060
<i>The enemy's still in this area!</i>

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:02.000
I heard your report.
You're sure, Chief?

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:05.770
Aye, sir. It was an improved
Zaku with three escorts.

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.140
We shot one of them down.

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:09.180
- And your people?
- Everyone but me was!

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:11.310
There are three more
enemies out there?!

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.280
That doesn't mean he should have
gone out in that piece of junk!

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:17.200
And again I lose
my place to stay...

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:18.040
Hm?

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:20.450
Nothing...How much air
does that guy have?

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:24.150
About...Two more hours
worth, I'd guess.

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:26.750
We can't keep waiting
around here, in any case.

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:29.360
Give him two hours, sir!
I'll look for him!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.280
It's hopeless.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:31.730
What's hopeless?!

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:35.330
We confirmed two explosions.
The Ball must have!

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:40.060
It was crazy, anyway.
Going out in that Ball.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:43.470
What would a guy who just
stood here watching know?!

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:45.710
I- I'm sorry, sir!

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:46.560
What?

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:49.910
Excuse me.
I withdraw the opinion!

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:53.820
Shoulda kept your mouth
shut to begin with!

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.400
<i>This is a Federal Forces ship.</i>

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.530
<i>It sure drifted</i>
<i>a long way out here.</i>

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:21.710
<i>There are still</i>
<i>sections with power!</i>

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:43.660
Hey, you!

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.310
God dammit!

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.180
<i>All this is doing</i>
<i>is using up my air!</i>

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:05.920
<i>What have I got to lose now?!</i>

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:26.340
I will not be a prisoner
of the Federal Forces.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:28.170
Shoot me now.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:31.820
C'mon. Can you stand up?

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.840
Don't touch me!

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:42.300
- Is it deep?
- It's just a scratch!

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:43.730
But if we don't
get that patched...

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:45.130
Get away from me!

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:48.640
Shut up and listen!
You want to die like that?!

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:51.000
C'mon!

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:51.970
Let me go!

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.340
We can't talk
unless I do this!

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:08.530
Come on, over here.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.510
You're REALLY pissing me off!

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:17.420
You're really
gonna die, you know?!

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:20.260
We have to conserve
every bit of air we have!

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:25.790
Here.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:28.300
Christ...

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:32.210
What did I do to deserve this?

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.440
Why are you helping me?

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:37.680
I don't know, either!

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:43.920
But you can't just give up!

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:45.980
You have to just think
about how to survive!

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.360
The air in here
won't last very long.

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:51.870
Did I wrap that too tight?

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:34.150
No luck here, either.

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:40.170
Hurry up. While we wait here,
we're just using up our air.

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:47.390
Can't see that Fed transport or
any Zeon mobile suits from here.

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:49.190
We've drifted a
long way off course.

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:50.060
Yeah.

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:57.300
Anyway, let's try
to find any radios...

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:59.370
...or signal flares
that may still be on board.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.600
We have to tell somebody
where we are.

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:02.230
Right.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:09.080
Okay, let's meet back
here in 10 minutes.

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:11.180
Gotcha.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.780
This is for my personal use.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:27.860
Whoa. Fancy watch you have there.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:30.230
Treat it gently, please.

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:31.300
Gotcha.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:31.310
- Well, let's hurry.
- Right.
Gotcha.

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:33.270
- Well, let's hurry.
- Right.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.680
<i>Okay, release those mooring lines!</i>

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:39.680
<i>Everyone who's finished with</i>
<i>their work, get back into the ship!</i>

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:41.640
C'mon, move it!

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:46.680
Even if that ensign's okay, his
air isn't going to last forever.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:47.900
We'll be finished soon!

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:49.840
<i>No way. There's no chance.</i>

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:51.530
<i>Propellant loading, complete!</i>

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:54.220
<i>Machine gun repair</i>
<i>and reload, complete!</i>

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:05.990
<i>There must be something</i>
<i>here to use. Something...</i>

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:12.300
No good!

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:19.960
That man...

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.090
This is awful...

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.540
That's!

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:44.470
We can use these!

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.140
Launch fireworks?

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:50.480
Exactly! If they
see an explosion...

00:17:50.550 --> 00:17:52.740
...they'll investigate
this area, right?

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:54.880
Don't knock it against
anything! Gently, now...

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.920
You got quite a brainstorm.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:05.760
I set the detonator for
a 3 second delay.

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.810
Nice job.

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:09.700
Maybe I should go into
the fireworks business.

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.060
Move back.

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:50.430
It really does
look like fireworks...

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.420
You're trembling, you know.

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:14.220
If nobody comes,
we're going to die here.

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:18.070
We'll be rescued.
I know we will!

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:25.620
I'm going down there.

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:26.960
For what?

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:30.490
Well, to fight, of course.

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:33.800
But, I think, if I go there,
I'll learn something.

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:38.070
Who I am and what
I'm capable of.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:41.160
So there's no way
I can die here!

00:19:41.710 --> 00:19:43.330
You're...

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:47.460
You're not how I pictured
a Feddie soldier would be.

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:52.450
I envy you.

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:54.800
Envy me?

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.740
Those are Zeon suits!

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.050
Let's go!

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.910
I don't want
to be a prisoner.

00:20:06.090 --> 00:20:09.280
But, if you stay here!
I can't just let you die!

00:20:10.090 --> 00:20:11.490
I'll be rescued, too.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:12.470
But!

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:14.520
Get going!

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:16.660
My name is Aina Sahalin!

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:19.480
Aina? My name's Shiro Amada.

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:21.190
Goodbye, Shiro.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:36.940
Glad to see you're all right.

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:39.060
Yeah. Thanks.

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:42.950
I'm just sad we lost the battle
data from the improved suit.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:49.550
Aina! Your watch! Aina!

00:20:57.450 --> 00:20:58.380
Uh-oh!

00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:03.400
No, it couldn't fight even if it
wanted to. Get us out of here.

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:04.560
Right!

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:10.680
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.380
<i>I don't believe him!</i>

00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:18.980
<i>He came back alive</i>
<i>after all that!</i>

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:20.860
<i>I'm gonna have to</i>
<i>rewrite my letter!</i>

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.790
Leave him alone, kid.

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:25.430
He's tired.

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:28.390
Chief Sanders! Uh, sir!

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:30.930
Calm down, kid.

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.150
Y- Yes, sir!

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:33.860
Excuse me, sir!

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:37.270
You see, sir...We just got
our orders a little while ago.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:39.900
You and I are assigned
to the same unit, Chief.

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:41.990
It's a pleasure
to meet you, sir.

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:49.220
<i>No time to ship me</i>
<i>back to my old unit...</i>

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:51.960
<i>Guess they want the</i>
<i>jinx out for good.</i>

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:56.920
And the commander of the
08th Team is that guy, there.

00:22:00.430 --> 00:22:04.670
<i>Maybe this ensign can</i>
<i>finally change my luck.</i>

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:08.590
Hey, the Zabis
are giving a speech!

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:10.070
What?

00:22:10.570 --> 00:22:12.800
Hey, isn't that
the Zeek big shot?

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:17.010
<i>No! We are only beginning!</i>
<i>How is it the Duchy of Zeon has...</i>

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:19.620
What's he saying,
the goddamn Zeek!

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:23.680
Thing is, I hear that a big
offensive's about to start.

00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:25.150
You gotta be kidding!

00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:28.750
Who cares?! We're gonna drive
those Zeon off of our Earth!

00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:30.260
Yeah, that's right!

00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:32.420
They better watch their step! Right?

00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:33.460
Yeah!

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:56.010
osanaikoro kara
All that time that's passed me by.

00:22:56.080 --> 00:22:59.700
sou kyou made no so many days
From childhood till now, so many days.

00:22:59.780 --> 00:23:03.840
furikaereba ironna
When I look back, I see so many things...

00:23:03.920 --> 00:23:07.610
koto ni meguriatta
...that happened to come into my life.

00:23:07.690 --> 00:23:10.780
naitari warattari
The times I cried, the times I laughed.

00:23:11.090 --> 00:23:14.790
kenka shitari yume mitari
The times I fought, the times I dreamed.

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:18.920
chotto hard na shitsuren mo
The lost loves that were sort of hard.

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:22.060
kagayaku my history
All shining in my history.

00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:25.200
ikutsumono
The ones who caused me pain...

00:23:25.270 --> 00:23:30.070
deai to wakare kugurinukete
...I met and left along the way.

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:35.940
ai suru anata ni sou yo
But I still ended up meeting you.

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:40.280
Love! meguriaeta
The one that I love.

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:45.180
Ten years after juunen go no
Ten years after, A decade from now.

00:23:45.290 --> 00:23:48.950
watashi wa doushiteru darou
I wonder what I will be doing then.

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:56.090
donna fuu ni anata o sukideiru darou
I wonder how I will be still loving you.

00:23:56.870 --> 00:24:00.200
Ten years after, juunen go no
Ten years after, a decade from now.

00:24:00.270 --> 00:24:04.270
anata o mitsumete mitai
I still want to be looking at you.

00:24:04.340 --> 00:24:08.010
Stay together sono toki
Stay together. When that day comes...

00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:14.700
kitto soba de hohoendeitai
...I want to be at your side with a smile.

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:26.510
I finally meet the 08th mobile
suit team as their new commander.

00:24:27.160 --> 00:24:30.890
But before I can even learn their
names, we're ordered into action!

00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:32.900
I can't say I'm not
a little nervous...

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:36.100
...but I want to show my team
that I'm able to lead them!

00:24:37.270 --> 00:24:41.140
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam -
The 08th MS Team:

00:24:41.210 --> 00:24:42.800
"Gundams in the Jungle."
